{"title":"Career Roadmap · Game Designer","role":"Game Designer","summary":"A Game Designer creates the rules, mechanics, systems, player experiences, levels, progression and overall structure of games. Unlike a game programmer, the designer primarily focuses on how the game works and how players experience it.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Toy & Game Design","Game Design Projects","Game Design Internship","Junior Game Designer","Game Designer","Senior Game Designer","Lead Game Designer","Game Director"]}]},{"heading":"What Does a Game Designer Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A game designer converts an idea into a playable experience."},{"type":"h","text":"Core responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Develop game concepts"},{"text":"Design gameplay mechanics"},{"text":"Create rules and systems"},{"text":"Design levels and environments"},{"text":"Create player progression"},{"text":"Balance difficulty"},{"text":"Design rewards and challenges"},{"text":"Develop game loops"},{"text":"Write game design documents"},{"text":"Prototype mechanics"},{"text":"Conduct playtests"},{"text":"Analyse player behaviour"},{"text":"Collaborate with programmers and artists"},{"text":"Refine gameplay based on feedback"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The game designer answers:"},{"type":"h","text":"“What does the player do, why is it fun, and how does the game respond?”"}]},{"heading":"Toy & Game Design Fit","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A B.Des in Toy & Game Design can be particularly useful because it develops understanding of:"},{"type":"table","header":["Area","Relevance"],"rows":[[{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Play experience"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"User psychology"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Visual design"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Interaction design"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Level design"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Physical games"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Digital games"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Creativity"},{"text":"Very High"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should build both physical and digital game-design projects."}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Game Design Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game theory"},{"text":"Design principles"},{"text":"Visual communication"},{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Character development"},{"text":"Basic psychology"},{"text":"Interaction design"},{"text":"Creative problem solving"},{"text":"Observation and user research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand game concepts"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rules"},{"text":"Goals"},{"text":"Challenges"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Player choice"},{"text":"Competition"},{"text":"Cooperation"},{"text":"Randomness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Board game"},{"text":"Card game"},{"text":"Puzzle game"},{"text":"Simple mobile-game concept"},{"text":"Game mechanic prototype"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Goal"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand why games are engaging, not just how they look."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Digital Game Design"},{"type":"p","text":"The student now moves toward digital game development."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Game loops"},{"text":"Level design"},{"text":"Player progression"},{"text":"Difficulty curves"},{"text":"Game economy"},{"text":"Narrative design"},{"text":"UX for games"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Playtesting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Game engines"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn at least one:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unity"},{"text":"Unreal Engine"},{"text":"Godot"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A designer does not necessarily need advanced programming, but should understand enough scripting to prototype ideas."},{"type":"h","text":"Useful programming"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"C# basics for Unity"},{"text":"Blueprint visual scripting in Unreal"},{"text":"GDScript basics for Godot"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Professional Game Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Level design"},{"text":"Systems design"},{"text":"Combat design"},{"text":"Quest design"},{"text":"Economy design"},{"text":"Progression systems"},{"text":"Multiplayer fundamentals"},{"text":"Game balancing"},{"text":"Narrative systems"},{"text":"Player retention"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Start professional projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Programmers"},{"text":"2D artists"},{"text":"3D artists"},{"text":"Animators"},{"text":"Sound designers"},{"text":"Writers"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is to learn cross-functional game development."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Portfolio & Industry Preparation"},{"type":"p","text":"The final year should focus heavily on portfolio quality."},{"type":"h","text":"Build"},{"type":"p","text":"2–3 polished playable games rather than 10 unfinished concepts."},{"type":"p","text":"Each project should show:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Game Idea","Player Problem / Experience","Core Mechanic","Prototype","Playtest","Iteration","Playable Build","Final Game"]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio should include"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game design documents"},{"text":"Gameplay videos"},{"text":"Playable prototypes"},{"text":"Level designs"},{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Game-flow diagrams"},{"text":"Wireframes"},{"text":"Playtesting results"},{"text":"Design iterations"},{"text":"Your specific contribution"}]}]},{"heading":"Core Game Design Concepts","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong game designer should understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Core loop"},{"type":"flow","items":["Action","Feedback","Reward","New Challenge","Action"]},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"p","text":"A player:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Explore","Fight","Collect","Upgrade","Explore"]},{"type":"p","text":"This loop keeps the gameplay moving."},{"type":"h","text":"Other important concepts"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game loop"},{"text":"Meta loop"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Difficulty curve"},{"text":"Risk/reward"},{"text":"Player agency"},{"text":"Feedback systems"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Resource management"},{"text":"Game economy"}]}]},{"heading":"Game Engines & Tools","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Engines"},{"type":"h","text":"Primary choice:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unreal Engine"},{"text":"Godot"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2D / visual design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"Illustrator"},{"text":"Figma"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3D"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"Maya"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Game documentation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Notion"},{"text":"Miro"},{"text":"Google Docs"},{"text":"Excel / Google Sheets"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Version control"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Git"},{"text":"GitHub"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A designer should be comfortable working inside the engine, even if they are not the primary programmer."}]},{"heading":"Game Design Documentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to create a Game Design Document (GDD)."},{"type":"p","text":"A GDD can contain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game concept"},{"text":"Target audience"},{"text":"Platform"},{"text":"Core gameplay"},{"text":"Game loop"},{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Characters"},{"text":"Levels"},{"text":"Controls"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Art direction"},{"text":"Audio"},{"text":"Monetisation"},{"text":"Technical requirements"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, the best portfolio demonstrates working prototypes, not documentation alone."}]},{"heading":"Level Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Level designers create the structure through which players experience gameplay."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Player navigation"},{"text":"Spatial flow"},{"text":"Pacing"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Environmental storytelling"},{"text":"Enemy placement"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Checkpoints"},{"text":"Exploration"},{"text":"Player guidance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"Recreate the level flow of an existing game and explain:"},{"type":"flow","items":["A","B","C?"],"label":"Why does the player move from"},{"type":"p","text":"Then create your own alternative."}]},{"heading":"Game Balancing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Game designers must understand how to balance:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Player power"},{"text":"Enemy power"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Resources"},{"text":"Currency"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Time"},{"text":"Risk"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Difficulty ↑","Challenge ↑","Skill Requirement ↑","Reward ↑"]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is to create meaningful challenge, not arbitrary difficulty."}]},{"heading":"Playtesting","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Playtesting is one of the most important professional skills."},{"type":"h","text":"Process"},{"type":"flow","items":["Prototype","Observe Player","Collect Feedback","Identify Problems","Change Mechanics","Test Again"]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to distinguish between:"},{"type":"p","text":"What players say\nand\nWhat players actually do."}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"College game projects"},{"text":"Game jams"},{"text":"Board-game projects"},{"text":"Indie teams"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Indie studios"},{"text":"Mobile-game startups"},{"text":"Game design internships"},{"text":"Game testing/QA teams"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3–4"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game studios"},{"text":"AAA studios"},{"text":"Mobile gaming companies"},{"text":"Console-game studios"},{"text":"VR/AR companies"},{"text":"Educational game companies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Game jams"},{"type":"p","text":"Participating in game jams is particularly useful because they demonstrate the ability to:"},{"type":"flow","items":["design","prototype","collaborate","deliver under time constraints"]}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Mobile Game"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a simple mobile game with a strong core loop."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Puzzle Game"},{"type":"p","text":"Demonstrate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Difficulty progression"},{"text":"Level design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Narrative Game"},{"type":"p","text":"Demonstrate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Story"},{"text":"Dialogue"},{"text":"Player choice"},{"text":"Branching narrative"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Multiplayer Prototype"},{"type":"p","text":"Demonstrate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Competitive/cooperative mechanics"},{"text":"Player interaction"},{"text":"Balancing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Board-to-Digital Game"},{"type":"p","text":"Take an original board game and transform it into a digital game."},{"type":"p","text":"This project is particularly relevant to a Toy & Game Design graduate."}]},{"heading":"Specialisations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After gaining fundamentals, a game designer can specialise in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Systems Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Player systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Level Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Levels"},{"text":"Environments"},{"text":"Pacing"},{"text":"Player flow"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Narrative Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Story"},{"text":"Dialogue"},{"text":"Characters"},{"text":"Player choices"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Combat Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Combat mechanics"},{"text":"Weapons"},{"text":"Enemies"},{"text":"Abilities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Economy Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Virtual currencies"},{"text":"Rewards"},{"text":"Progression"},{"text":"Monetisation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"UX Designer for Games"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Menus"},{"text":"Controls"},{"text":"Information architecture"},{"text":"Player usability"}]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful learning areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game design"},{"text":"Unity"},{"text":"Unreal Engine"},{"text":"Level design"},{"text":"Game UX"},{"text":"Narrative design"},{"text":"3D modelling"},{"text":"Game development"},{"text":"Interactive storytelling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But again:"},{"type":"h","text":"Playable projects > certificates"},{"type":"p","text":"For a game-design recruiter, a strong playable prototype can be considerably more useful than a long certificate list."}]},{"heading":"Interview Questions","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Fundamentals"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What makes a game fun?"},{"text":"What is a core gameplay loop?"},{"text":"What is game balance?"},{"text":"What is player agency?"},{"text":"What is level design?"},{"text":"What is progression?"},{"text":"What is a game economy?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"How would you make a boring mechanic interesting?"},{"text":"How would you design the first level of a game?"},{"text":"How would you balance an overpowered character?"},{"text":"How would you improve player retention?"},{"text":"How would you test whether a mechanic is working?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design challenge"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a simple game using only one button."},{"type":"p","text":"A strong candidate should quickly explain:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Goal","Mechanic","Rules","Feedback","Difficulty","Progression"]}]},{"heading":"Higher Education Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible postgraduate directions:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Des Game Design"},{"text":"M.Des Interaction Design"},{"text":"MA Game Design"},{"text":"MSc Game Development"},{"text":"Game Design specialisation"},{"text":"Interactive Media"},{"text":"UX/Interaction Design"},{"text":"Animation & Interactive Design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A master's degree is not mandatory if the student already has a strong portfolio and industry experience."}]},{"heading":"Related Careers","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The degree can also lead to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game Designer"},{"text":"Level Designer"},{"text":"Systems Designer"},{"text":"Narrative Designer"},{"text":"Quest Designer"},{"text":"Combat Designer"},{"text":"Game UX Designer"},{"text":"Game Producer"},{"text":"Game Writer"},{"text":"Game Tester"},{"text":"Technical Game Designer"},{"text":"Game Design Researcher"},{"text":"Creative Director"}]}]},{"heading":"AI & Future of Game Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI is changing game development rapidly."},{"type":"p","text":"A modern game designer should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted prototyping"},{"text":"Procedural content generation"},{"text":"Generative environments"},{"text":"AI NPC behaviour"},{"text":"Dynamic dialogue"},{"text":"Adaptive difficulty"},{"text":"AI-assisted concept development"},{"text":"Automated playtesting"},{"text":"Player-behaviour analysis"},{"text":"Generative assets"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Future games may increasingly respond dynamically to individual players."},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Player Behaviour","AI Analysis","Difficulty / Content Adaptation","Personalised Game Experience"]},{"type":"p","text":"The designer's role therefore shifts toward designing intelligent systems and player experiences, not merely fixed game rules."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Experience","Typical Role"],"rows":[[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Junior Game Designer"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Game Designer"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Game Designer"}],[{"text":"7–10 years"},{"text":"Lead Game Designer"}],[{"text":"10+ years"},{"text":"Game Director"}],[{"text":"Senior Leadership"},{"text":"Creative Director"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Progression varies substantially between indie, mobile, AAA and startup studios."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"flow","items":["Game Mechanics","Systems Design","Level Design"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Creative"},{"type":"flow","items":["Storytelling","Narrative","Visual Design"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"flow","items":["Unity/Unreal","Basic Scripting","Prototyping"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Analytical"},{"type":"flow","items":["Game Balancing","Player Analytics","Playtesting"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"flow","items":["Communication","Collaboration","Documentation","Problem Solving"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Future"},{"type":"flow","items":["AI","Procedural Generation","Adaptive Gameplay","XR"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Target Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Toy & Game Design","Game Design Portfolio","Game Jams + Prototypes","Game Design Internship","Junior Game Designer","Game Designer","Senior Game Designer","Lead Game Designer","Game Director","Creative Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, an ideal B.Des Toy & Game Design → Game Designer candidate should have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"🎮 2–3 polished playable games"},{"text":"🧩 Strong understanding of game mechanics"},{"text":"🗺️ Level-design experience"},{"text":"📄 Game Design Documents"},{"text":"🧪 Multiple playtesting iterations"},{"text":"⚖️ Game-balancing knowledge"},{"text":"🖥️ Unity/Unreal/Godot experience"},{"text":"💻 Basic scripting ability"},{"text":"🎨 Understanding of game art pipelines"},{"text":"📊 Basic player analytics knowledge"},{"text":"🤝 Experience working with multidisciplinary teams"},{"text":"🏆 Game-jam or competition experience"},{"text":"🤖 Awareness of AI-assisted game development"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Ideal graduate profile","text":"“A designer who can take a game idea from concept to a playable prototype, explain the design decisions behind it, test it with real players, and iteratively improve the experience.”"}]}]}